# Track 4 — E2E round 3: 40 vCPU total budget
#
# Rebalanced after docker stats showed the token-issuer (RS256 signing) pinned
# at its cap while validators sat at ~5%. Budget moved validators -> issuer,
# with the request-handler kept matched so it isn't the next bottleneck.
#
# | Service              | cpus x replicas | subtotal |
# |----------------------|-----------------|----------|
# | Redis x 3            | 0.2 x 3         | 0.6      |
# | request-handler      | 0.8 x 4         | 3.2      |
# | verifier-selector    | 0.7 x 1         | 0.7      |
# | token-issuer         | 1.0 x 4         | 4.0      |
# | snark-verifier       | 1.0 x 30        | 30.0     |
# | token-validator (x5) | 0.3 x 5         | 1.5      |
# | TOTAL                |                 | 40.0     |
#
# issuer (~880/s) and handler (~880/s) are balanced; verifiers (30) could do
# ~1260/s, so the token pipeline is still the ceiling but ~1.7x the old config.
# token-validator 0.3 covers each domain's 60% hot window (rotating focus).
#
# Load with:  set -a; source e2e-throughput-round3.env; set +a
REDIS_CPUS=0.2
HANDLER_REPLICAS=4
HANDLER_CPUS=0.8
SELECTOR_CPUS=0.7
ISSUER_REPLICAS=4
ISSUER_CPUS=1.0
SNARK_REPLICAS=30
SNARK_COUNT=30
# Applied manually on each App EC2: docker update --cpus=$VALIDATOR_CPUS ...
VALIDATOR_CPUS=0.3
